c, which completes the proof of Theorem. 3.


6 Finding Long Paths in Most Sparse Digraphs
In this section we show that in a sparse expander graph, a relatively long path
is easily found. These ideas are inspired by the analysis of the low expected
time for finding a Hamiltonian cycle in a random graph [2, 8].
    A digraph G = (V, A) on n vertices is a c-expander if |δU | ≥ c(1 − |Un | )|U |
for every subset U ⊂ V where δU = { v ∈    / U | ∃u ∈ U : uv ∈ A }. A standard
probabilistic argument shows that with high probability a random digraphs with
outdegree k (k > 2), are ck -expanders for some constant ck , for large enough
n > nk . In other words, the result holds for most bounded outdegree graphs.
    We propose the following algorithm for finding a long path p0 · · · pl in a
sparse expander.
